From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] apklayer: readdir-per-thread

readdir: the entry it returns lives in a buffer per thread, not one for the process, and the entries "." and ".." are not returned. Gecko lists directories on several threads at once, and its recursive scan of the safebrowsing directory (Classifier::ScanStoreDir) followed "./././..." until the stack was gone, so the dot entries do not reach the callers that forget to skip them.

apklayer patch: step 16 of the former scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh (see docs/PATCHES.md), patch 0021 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
 libc/libc.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libc/libc.c b/libc/libc.c
index 88832fc..e5a1ece 100644
--- a/libc/libc.c
+++ b/libc/libc.c
@@ -249,10 +249,12 @@ struct bionic_dirent *
 bionic_readdir(DIR *dirp)
 {
 	assert(dirp);
-	static struct bionic_dirent bde;
+	static __thread struct bionic_dirent bde; /* apklayer patch: see scripts/patch-bionic-translation.sh step 16 */
 	struct dirent *de;
-	if (!(de = readdir(dirp)))
-		return NULL;
+	do {
+		if (!(de = readdir(dirp)))
+			return NULL;
+	} while (!strcmp(de->d_name, ".") || !strcmp(de->d_name, ".."));
 	glibc_dirent_to_bionic_dirent(de, &bde);
 	return &bde;
 }
